```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class MemberFinder {
    // Linear search of a name in a list of six members, ignoring the case of the letters
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String[] m = new String[6];
        for (int i = 0; i < m.length; i++)
            m[i] = sc.next();
        String key = sc.next();
        int pos = -1;
        for (int i = 0; i < m.length; i++) {
            if (m[i].equalsIgnoreCase(key)) {
                pos = i;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (pos == -1)
            System.out.println(key + " is not in the list");
        else
            System.out.println(key + " is at position " + (pos + 1));
    }
}
```

**Sample input:** `Ishaan Devika Rohit Anaya Kabir Sneha ROHIT`

**Output:**

```
ROHIT is at position 3
```

**Another run, input** `Ishaan Devika Rohit Anaya Kabir Sneha Mohan`**:**

```
Mohan is not in the list
```

**Variable description**

| Variable | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| m | String[] | array of the six member names |
| key | String | name to be searched |
| pos | int | index of the match, -1 while no match is found |
| i | int | loop variable |

